# src/syncai_camera_feeder, from SyncAI-Robot-Camera-Feeder: the node meant to be
# the single owner of /dev/syncai/camera0, fanning its MJPEG stream out as
# localhost RTP/JPEG (for the WebRTC worker) and as sensor_msgs/CompressedImage
# (for ROS). Managed with vcstool, the same way lio-bridge.repos manages
# src/syncai_lio_bridge, robot-state.repos manages src/syncai_robot_state,
# driver-manager.repos manages src/syncai_driver_manager, interface.repos
# manages src/syncai_common and third-party.repos manages src/third-party/.
#
#   vcs import < camera-feeder.repos          # populate a fresh clone
#   vcs import < camera-feeder.repos --force  # re-checkout after changing the pin
#
# The key already carries `src/`, so run this from the workspace root without an
# extra `src` argument, or the package lands in `src/src/`.
#
# Unlike the other three Rust packages it never lived in this repository: it is
# new, written against rclrs (Rust, `ament_cargo`) from the start. It is in no
# session spec yet, so importing it changes nothing at runtime -- the camera is
# still owned by the host-side scripts/publish_camera_crop.sh, and exactly one
# process may hold the V4L2 device (see "Camera" in CLAUDE.md). Wiring it into a
# session means retiring that script, not running beside it.
#
# `src/syncai_camera_feeder/` is gitignored -- edit the node in that checkout
# (its own git repo) and commit there, never here; the next --force import
# overwrites anything uncommitted.
#
# Tracks `feat/camera-feeder`, NOT `dev` like the other first-party .repos
# files: the node exists only on that branch so far (`dev` and `main` predate
# it). Move this to `dev` once the branch has merged there.
#
# HTTPS rather than the SSH remote: the repo is public, so the build container
# needs no keys. `git@github.com:chungweeeei/SyncAI-Robot-Camera-Feeder.git` is
# the same checkout for anyone who prefers to push over SSH.
#
# Like the other three, its Rust message crates (builtin_interfaces /
# sensor_msgs / std_msgs) come from the image's ros2-rust underlay
# (/opt/ros2_rust_underlay) -- see driver-manager.repos and the Dockerfile's
# underlay stanza. What it needs beyond them is GStreamer: the `gstreamer` /
# `gstreamer-app` crates find it through pkg-config, so libgstreamer1.0-dev and
# libgstreamer-plugins-base1.0-dev must be in the image (the Dockerfile stanza
# right after the underlay). Its crates are pinned to the `v1_20` feature on
# purpose -- the image is Ubuntu 22.04 with GStreamer 1.20.
repositories:
  src/syncai_camera_feeder:
    type: git
    url: https://github.com/chungweeeei/SyncAI-Robot-Camera-Feeder.git
    version: feat/camera-feeder
